#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a74d2eb-fe22-5c2d-b31f-9446f8f080d3" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Union of Overlapping Intervals"}] :question/id #uuid "9cf4daed-1d80-5a74-90dc-b0b1da0ce6b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-1695" :question/problem "Simplify the union of intervals $(-\\infty,2) \\cup [-1,3]$." :question/worked-solution "If we plot these two intervals on number lines, we get the following:\n\n![](images/27/2720cafe76aff8eb85ca65851570087505ee57a4b51904ee075aa86436cfc475.png)\n\n![](images/c3/c379dc0e0c371832a53e62da4505cfc0b03df50efc7241c0100794a191c8fb97.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/c4/c43257d8d30711804848039b3b8458302e0030e7512fb7cbf1f4b697263e5155.png)\n\nThis graph represents the interval $(-\\infty,3]$. So, the union $(-\\infty,2) \\cup [-1,3]$ simplifies to the interval $(-\\infty,3]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068631 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6619614-04df-5a22-afa8-77a41b016330" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Union of Overlapping Intervals Given Graphically"}] :question/id #uuid "489ef834-7015-5592-a5f5-b0daa3bc9f7b" :question/math-academy-id "e-6278" :question/problem "What is the union of the intervals shown on the number lines below?\n\n![](images/60/603da954fd0e711ffa4879c51db847095edd9b1f256bbef66ad9de91c8cb31b4.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have the following number lines:\n\n![](images/60/603da954fd0e711ffa4879c51db847095edd9b1f256bbef66ad9de91c8cb31b4.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/58/5829d80a75446161fba99c08b361083a025a0c341fa41cf0608867d220dfa538.png)\n\nThe graph represents the interval $(-1,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068666 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068811 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eee95dd4-7d0c-5c18-bcb0-9b033e0cb509" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Inequality as a Union of Intervals"}] :question/id #uuid "d0e51ce4-7f83-545e-9c3c-b79bf58d0eab" :question/math-academy-id "e-952" :question/problem "Express the compound inequality $x < 4$ or $x \\ge 10$ using interval notation." :question/worked-solution "We can represent the compound inequality on a number line, as follows:\n\n![](images/26/26594fb87ed7eca0803d554e4a1fbd3d3719cc01ba4e70f96126b73924ac5769.png)\n\nThis number line consists of the interval $(-\\infty, 4)$ as well as the interval $[10, \\infty)$.\n\nSo, we can express the compound inequality as the union of these two intervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty, 4) \\:{\\cup}\\: [10, \\infty)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068667 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1300ab0b-313f-5489-a836-79cf200082f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Union of Non-Overlapping Intervals as an Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "c575830c-0100-5cec-a3f8-70e29cba3b54" :question/math-academy-id "e-954" :question/problem "Express $\\left(-\\infty, -1 \\right) \\cup [2, \\infty)$ as an inequality." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the two intervals on a number line:\n\n![](images/eb/ebc7db3faf2d9eafb887e93e9cf3613853914bf02ef87b6f63b638494c55a2ac.png)\n\nThe interval\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\infty, -1 \\right)\n$$\n\ncan be expressed as the inequality $x < -1$.\n\nLikewise, the interval $[2, \\infty)$ can be expressed as the inequality\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2\n$$\n\nSo, the union of these intervals represents the compound inequality\n\n$$\nx < -1 \\text{or} x \\geq 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6619614-04df-5a22-afa8-77a41b016330" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Union of Overlapping Intervals Given Graphically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2d0e2e6-4da6-55ad-a378-e97707338113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- 5,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067295} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7dd19e-cecd-5b63-845d-915d330388a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067296} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3403b3-0adf-591d-9849-1299624c2430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- 5, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067297} {:answer/id #uuid "41898364-05ed-5cf2-b684-086570d8a81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067298} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1f8d50-23a2-58e3-8a12-5844bc0c7dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, 5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067299}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ac136aa4-1b65-52f8-bc74-b0768bda5857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067294}] :question/id #uuid "e818c059-b2ba-57e5-8dad-9805a5c081f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-44865" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e68b6cd55df9e2c81409910829e2194576a5e249a171c34ff28e30e3d34cb807.png)\n\nWhat is the union of the intervals shown on the number lines above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a74d2eb-fe22-5c2d-b31f-9446f8f080d3" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a